Reflection Questions

1. How did using Figma designs as references affect your coding process?
Using Figma designs as references helped me understand how professional websites are planned and structured before coding begins. The designs provided a visual guide for elements such as layout, spacing, colors, fonts, and alignment.

2. What challenges did you encounter when aligning your code with the design specifications?
One of the main challenges I had was getting the spacing, positioning, sizing, and alignment of elements to match the original design. I also had to understand how CSS properties such as padding, margin, width, height, and flexbox affect the appearance of a webpage.

3. How can the feedback and community resources on Frontend Mentor help you improve as a developer?
The Frontend Mentor feedback and community resources can help me to identify mistakes, learn better coding practices, and also learn alternative ways of solving development problems.

